cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HistoWeave in your research, please cite both the software and the original method implementations it orchestrates."
title: "HistoWeave: evidence-governed method decisions with structured abstention for spatial transcriptomics"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "HistoWeave contributors"
    website: "https://github.com/HERRY423/Histoweave"
version: 0.1.2
date-released: 2026-08-01
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/HERRY423/Histoweave"
url: "https://HERRY423.github.io/Histoweave"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21586217
abstract: >
  HistoWeave implements an executable evidence-governance and selective-decision
  protocol for spatial transcriptomics. Task, ground-truth, cluster-count policy,
  metric, panel, holdout, and source-hash contracts gate method decisions with
  fail-closed actions (personalised set, global default, evidence required, or
  abstain). The submission freeze packages a Bioinformatics Original Paper draft
  with dual-track oracle-K sensitivity, diagnostic ranking, selective
  regret-coverage, and two registered non-oracle external studies with a strict
  nine-method same-mask panel spanning 13 units. The real-study policies remain
  fail-closed and do not establish personalised superiority; positive selection
  is demonstrated only as fixed-split synthetic construct validity. The software
  also provides plugin orchestration, multi-dataset evidence packages, and
  reproducible benchmarks.
keywords:
  - spatial transcriptomics
  - bioinformatics
  - evidence governance
  - method selection
  - selective prediction
  - abstention
  - reproducibility
  - benchmarking
  - scverse
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Transcriptome-scale spatial gene expression in the human dorsolateral prefrontal cortex"
    authors:
      - family-names: Maynard
        given-names: Kristen R.
      - family-names: Collado-Torres
        given-names: Leonardo
    journal: Nature Neuroscience
    year: 2021
    doi: 10.1038/s41593-020-00787-0
    description: >
      Source of the DLPFC reference dataset used in HistoWeave benchmarks.
      Please cite this paper when using dlpfc_151507 data.
